# Copy to .env and fill in every value, then `docker compose up --build`.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored; this file is not, so nothing usable goes in it. Every
# value below is blank: an example that shipped a working password or a working
# signing key would be the very thing it exists to prevent.

# --- the gateway's JWT signing key ---------------------------------------------
# The one genuinely secret value here. Generate a fresh one:
#
#   openssl rand -base64 48
#
# The gateway refuses a key shorter than 32 bytes (HS256 needs a key at least
# that long), so too short a value is a startup failure with a message saying
# so, not a silently weaker signature. Tokens signed with one key are not
# accepted by a gateway configured with another, so changing it logs everybody
# out.
JWT_SECRET=

# --- demo login passwords ------------------------------------------------------
# The demo callers in application.yml (customer / organizer / admin) take their
# passwords from here so that no committed file holds a credential. Any value
# you like; they are not compared against anything stored, because there is no
# password store yet. The README's examples use <your DEMO_..._PASSWORD>
# placeholders, so whatever you choose is the value to substitute there.
#
# Every one of these must be set, including for a local run: the gateway
# refuses to start rather than start with a caller nobody can authenticate as.
DEMO_CUSTOMER_PASSWORD=
DEMO_ORGANIZER_PASSWORD=
DEMO_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
